    <string name="recommended_actions">Recommended Actions</string>
    <string name="recommended_actions_body">
        • Rinse &amp; Retest: Rinse your mouth with water and retest in\n\t
          30–60 minutes, avoiding food or acidic drinks beforehand.\n
        • Hydrate: Drinking water helps restore saliva’s natural buffering\n\t
          ability.\n
        • Notice Patterns: Frequent low pH readings may be associated\n\t
          with acid reflux, dry mouth, or dietary habits.\n
        • Seek Care if Persistent: Frequent acidity may increase the risk\n\t
          of enamel erosion and oral discomfort; consider consulting a\n\t
          dentist or healthcare provider if you experience persistent\n\t
          acidic readings, tooth sensitivity, or heartburn.
    </string>

